s=\"col-sm-12\">\r\n<div class=\"card\">\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<h3 class=\"card-title text-align-center\">Index of Learning Styles</h3>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"card-text text-align-center\"><a class=\"btn btn-info file file\" href=\"https://www.webtools.ncsu.edu/learningstyles/\" target=\"_blank\">Go to the Index of Learning Styles</a></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div id=\"contact\" class=\"contact-cube\">\r\n<h3>CONTACT:</h3>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Titus O'Rourke</strong><br />\r\n<em>Transition Specialist</em><br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:titus.orourke@maine.gov\">Titus.Orourke@maine.gov</a><br />\r\n207-215-6303</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\n<p class=\"doe-jump\"><a href=\"#contact\">Contact</a></p>\n<p class=\"doe-top\"><a href=\"#top\">Back to top</a></p>","notes":[],"decisions":[{"id":"emailcase","on":true,"label":"Write the email addresses the same way","why":"1 address is shown in whatever case it was typed in. The house form capitalises each name and leaves a middle initial in lower case — titus.orourke@maine.gov → Titus.Orourke@maine.gov. Only the first letter of each part changes, so a name that spells itself LaBreck keeps doing so.","value":"1 address"},{"id":"cardtitles","on":true,"label":"Put the card titles on one level","why":"7 card titles are written at a level copied from an example rather than chosen — h5 on a page whose sections are h2. Only the number changes.","value":"7 titles"},{"id":"buttons","on":true,"label":"Put the buttons on the house style","why":"7 buttons use a Bootstrap variant rather than btn-info, so the same kind of action is drawn three different ways across the site. Only the class changes.","value":"7 buttons"},{"id":"solo","on":true,"label":"Let a lone card use the full width","why":"1 row holds a single card in a part-width column, so it takes a third or a half of the page and the rest is blank. A row of one is not a grid.","value":"1 card"},{"id":"contacttitle","on":true,"label":"Set a job title the way the rest of the site does","why":"1 job title sits in plain text under the person's name, where 186 elsewhere on the site are in italics — so the same contact block is drawn two ways depending on the page, and the title runs into the name above it. The standard here is the site's own, not a preference: two thirds of these blocks already do it. No word changes.","value":"1 title"},{"id":"banner-graphic","on":true,"label":"Retire the old banner graphic","why":"It repeats the page title in picture form, which the new banner already does in type.","removes":"Banner 1 Primary.png"},{"id":"capheadings","on":true,"label":"Bring every heading up to h3 or above","why":"1 heading sat at h4 or deeper inside a card, a callout, a contact block or an accordion panel — components the outline walk leaves alone because they label a thing rather than a section. A reader using a screen reader still hears the level, so a fourth-level title inside a page that only goes to three is announced as belonging to a level that does not exist. Each is styled by its class and its position rather than its number, so nothing changes on screen.","value":"1 heading"},{"id":"eyebrow","on":true,"label":"Eyebrow: \"Transition - Young Person\"","why":"Taken from the parent page, /learning/specialed/transition/youngperson."}],"mechanical":["white-on-white text: 1","image alignment translated to the house class: 7","drupal entity attrs stripped: 31","target set by destination: 7","columns that never stack given a breakpoint: 7"],"findings":[{"name":"image-alone-between-sections","n":3,"eg":["I want to continue my education.","I want to explore career opportunities."]},{"name":"card-row-holding-one-card","n":2,"eg":["a grid row with one card in it","a grid row with one card in it"]},{"name":"heading-in-all-capitals","n":1,"eg":["CONTACT:"]}],"safe":true,"audit":{"alias":"/learning/specialed/transition/youngperson/idontknow","title":"Transition - Don't Know Yet","changed":"2026-04-06T23:22:55+00:00","words":5